Package: ShinyCEA
Title: Shiny Application for Cost-Effectiveness Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Carlos", "Pineda-Antunez", , "carlospinedant@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An R package with a Shiny application designed for teaching and
    applied research in cost-effectiveness analysis (CEA). Supports multiple
    model structures (e.g., Markov, Partitioned Survival) and allows analysts
    to perform deterministic and probabilistic evaluations. Features include
    parameter upload/editing, sensitivity analyses (DSA/PSA), publication-ready
    plots (Tornado, CE Plane, Frontier, CEAC), downloadable results, and
    automated report generation. Users can plug in custom models with minimal
    code via the new_cea_model() interface.
